<title>USA: High pressure to dominate Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>High pressure to dominate Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A warm ridge of high pressure building out of northeast Brazil into the coffee belt is expected to bring mild temperatures and no threat of damaging cold to the region, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Thursday.</p>
<p>According to WSC, this high pressure system should dominate the coffee belt for the next seven days.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed in the region this morning. Low temperatures ranged from 55-61 F (13-16 C).</p>
<p>Mostly fair skies will continue for the rest of today. Variably cloudy skies are expected for tomorrow and Saturday. Temperatures should be near to above normal levels with lows in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>The extended outlook calls for fair to partly cloudy skies through the beginning of next week with temperatures remaining near to above normal.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
